    simple_web_textarea_overlay_review_hard_stop_2026-07-27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: verified both doc blockers at tip. B1 (Draw IR painter imports the CPU framebuffer owner - reversed owner graph): STILL PRESENT (paint_draw_ir imported ~30 paint_raster symbols) - FIXED by extracting the renderer-neutral text-control owner: new simple_web_html_layout_renderer_paint_text_control.spl (559 lines) holds all text-control paint/clip helpers moved verbatim from the CPU painter (input_text_paint_plan(_with_overlay), InputTextPaintPlan/InputTextVisualMap, caret/selection colors, password masking, input_accepts_text_overlay, input_text_prefix, input_value_vector_x, input_text_glyph_advance, checkable_author_box_hidden, shared html_image_fit_size) depending only on layout text metrics + paint_primitives/paint_gradients_text (neutral clip/transform owners) + text facades - no framebuffer, no Draw IR, no rt_* externs, no any; paint_raster 2952 to 2419 lines with every re-export chain preserved (export use of the neutral owner); paint_draw_ir now imports the neutral owner + layout owner + primitives and dropped the raster import (plus two genuinely unused imports). B2 (browser_text_control.spl private rt_text_to_bytes/rt_bytes_to_text externs): MOOT - that file never landed; no such externs anywhere in current owners; both direct-runtime guards PASS - pinned by the new spec. Spec test/01_unit/browser_engine/paint_text_control_owner_graph_spec.spl 7/7 PASS (3 runs): neither owner imports the other, both consume the neutral owner, moved helpers live there, no-private-rt_text_to_bytes discipline, html_image_fit_size/INPUT_PASSWORD_MASK_GLYPH parity. Neighbours: input_text_overlay_plan_contract 12/1 (identical to HEAD baseline - the 1 is the spec's own documented known-RED), input_overflow_clip_chrome159 5/5 PASS, simple_web_input_overlay identical to baseline (5 pre-existing seed gaps unchanged). Warnings 801 vs 802 baseline (one fewer; rest re-attributed visibility class, no new kinds). direct-env-runtime-guard --working and --staged both PASS. Residuals (owner/feature lane per the doc's resume contract): the textarea MULTILINE overlay feature itself (raw descendant text, CRLF mapping, per-line alignment/RTL, scroll state, newline-only selection) needs a fresh feature lane + admitted runtime + independent review - flipping the single-line gate without the plan would mis-render textarea, deliberately not done; the 800-line compat-owner cap vs the 1982-line aggregator is an owner decision; a pre-existing load-order-dependent circular import (backend_vulkan cycle) observed once, not reproducible in 6+ runs - engine2d owners should break it. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/browser_engine/paint_text_control_owner_graph_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/browser_engine/input_text_overflow_clip_chrome159_spec.spl"

